{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unstable-vitriolic-conch","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAt the audited snapshot, `src/rebar/llm/config.py` was 799 lines and `LLMConfig.from_env` occupied lines 566-768. ADR 0056 and closed ticket `candied-senseless-squirrel` anticipated this next headroom breach.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep `LLMConfig.from_env` as the sole precedence and composition facade. Extract cohesive table-driven readers for model/provider, budgets, tracing, web, and path settings into focused sibling modules. Preserve current precedence, validation, defaults, and patch-visible exports during this extraction; the separately ADR-gated internal-shim work may later migrate private compatibility paths.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py`\n- focused LLM configuration reader siblings\n- `tests/unit/test_config_llm.py` and config precedence/patch tests\n\nCascade flag: true. Recensus semantic, string, dynamic-import, environment, and monkeypatch references.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse table-driven cases for config-file, environment, explicit override, malformed value, missing value, and cross-field precedence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Model/provider, budget, tracing, web, and path parsing are owned by cohesive readers without duplicating precedence logic.\n- [ ] `LLMConfig.from_env` remains the only composition/precedence facade.\n- [ ] Existing defaults, validation failures, environment/config precedence, and patch-visible behavior are byte/value equivalent.\n- [ ] Focused config tests plus module-size, complexity, lint, and typecheck gates pass.","id":"86c0-59ec-a28b-4f7c","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","llm","refactor","rp13"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Extract cohesive table-driven LLM configuration readers"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788311604193270001,"uuid":"6661aeee-844e-4627-8506-2f5236a66274"}